# The source distribution: the package, its examples and its tests, and the
# texts beside them. The wheel carries the package alone.
#
# An allow-list. The examples are listed by name, so whatever a person or a
# run leaves in examples/ is never packed: a copy of a notebook, Jupyter's
# checkpoint folder (which keeps a notebook's outputs and a key typed into a
# cell), notes, scans, results, a record and its lock file. Build releases
# from a commit, never from a working folder.
include LICENSE README.md SECURITY.md CHANGELOG.md pyproject.toml MANIFEST.in
recursive-include src/nalvera *.py *.json
recursive-include tests *.py
# Generated by tests/examples_helpers.py from the examples' indexes: each by name.
include examples/README.md
include examples/anonymize_only.py
